# 高频词汇 List02 单词

## assume
- **音标**: /əˈsuːm/
- **词性**: vt.
- **释义**: 假定；承担
- **例句**: I assume you agree with the plan.
- **近义词**: presume, suppose
- **派生词**: assumption

## assure
- **音标**: /əˈʃʊr/
- **词性**: vt.
- **释义**: 向…保证；确保
- **例句**: I assure you everything will be fine.
- **近义词**: guarantee, promise
- **派生词**: assurance

## attach
- **音标**: /əˈtætʃ/
- **词性**: vt.
- **释义**: 附上；依恋
- **例句**: Please attach your photo to the form.
- **近义词**: fasten, connect
- **派生词**: attachment

## attain
- **音标**: /əˈteɪn/
- **词性**: vt.
- **释义**: 达到；获得
- **例句**: She attained the highest score.
- **近义词**: achieve, reach
- **派生词**: attainment

## attempt
- **音标**: /əˈtempt/
- **词性**: vt./n.
- **释义**: 尝试；企图
- **例句**: He attempted to escape.
- **近义词**: try, endeavor

## attribute
- **音标**: /əˈtrɪbjuːt/
- **词性**: vt./n.
- **释义**: 归因于；属性
- **例句**: He attributed his success to hard work.
- **近义词**: ascribe, credit
- **派生词**: attribution

## authority
- **音标**: /əˈθɔːrəti/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 权威；当局
- **例句**: She is an authority on linguistics.
- **近义词**: power, jurisdiction
- **派生词**: authoritative

## automatic
- **音标**: /ˌɔːtəˈmætɪk/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 自动的；无意识的
- **例句**: The door has an automatic lock.
- **近义词**: self-operating, mechanical
- **派生词**: automatically

## available
- **音标**: /əˈveɪləbl/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 可用的；有空的
- **例句**: Is this seat available?
- **近义词**: accessible, obtainable
- **派生词**: availability

## benefit
- **音标**: /ˈbenɪfɪt/
- **词性**: n./v.
- **释义**: 利益；有益于
- **例句**: Exercise benefits your health.
- **近义词**: advantage, profit
- **派生词**: beneficial

## bias
- **音标**: /ˈbaɪəs/
- **词性**: n./v.
- **释义**: 偏见；偏向
- **例句**: The report shows a clear bias.
- **近义词**: prejudice, partiality
- **派生词**: biased

## boast
- **音标**: /boʊst/
- **词性**: v./n.
- **释义**: 夸耀；自夸
- **例句**: He boasted about his achievement.
- **近义词**: brag, show off

## boost
- **音标**: /buːst/
- **词性**: vt./n.
- **释义**: 促进；增加
- **例句**: The new policy boosted the economy.
- **近义词**: increase, enhance

## boundary
- **音标**: /ˈbaʊndri/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 边界；界限
- **例句**: The river forms the boundary between the two countries.
- **近义词**: border, limit

## capable
- **音标**: /ˈkeɪpəbl/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 有能力的；能干的
- **例句**: She is capable of handling the task.
- **近义词**: competent, able
- **派生词**: capability

## capture
- **音标**: /ˈkæptʃər/
- **词性**: vt./n.
- **释义**: 捕获；夺取
- **例句**: The photographer captured a beautiful moment.
- **近义词**: seize, catch

## casual
- **音标**: /ˈkæʒuəl/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 随便的；非正式的
- **例句**: He wore casual clothes to the party.
- **近义词**: informal, relaxed
- **派生词**: casually

## cease
- **音标**: /siːs/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 停止；终止
- **例句**: The factory ceased production.
- **近义词**: stop, halt
- **派生词**: ceaseless

## challenge
- **音标**: /ˈtʃælɪndʒ/
- **词性**: n./v.
- **释义**: 挑战；质疑
- **例句**: This is a real challenge for us.
- **近义词**: dare, contest
- **派生词**: challenging

## circumstance
- **音标**: /ˈsɜːrkəmstæns/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 情况；环境
- **例句**: Under no circumstances should you give up.
- **近义词**: condition, situation

## collapse
- **音标**: /kəˈlæps/
- **词性**: v./n.
- **释义**: 倒塌；崩溃
- **例句**: The building collapsed during the earthquake.
- **近义词**: fall, crumble

## commit
- **音标**: /kəˈmɪt/
- **词性**: vt.
- **释义**: 犯（罪）；承诺
- **例句**: He committed a serious crime.
- **近义词**: pledge, dedicate
- **派生词**: commitment

## communicate
- **音标**: /kəˈmjuːnɪkeɪt/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 沟通；传达
- **例句**: They communicate in English.
- **近义词**: convey, express
- **派生词**: communication

## compete
- **音标**: /kəmˈpiːt/
- **词性**: vi.
- **释义**: 竞争；比赛
- **例句**: Several companies competed for the contract.
- **近义词**: contend, rival
- **派生词**: competition, competitive

## complex
- **音标**: /ˈkɑːmpleks/
- **词性**: adj./n.
- **释义**: 复杂的；综合体
- **例句**: This is a complex problem.
- **近义词**: complicated, intricate
- **派生词**: complexity
